<title>USA: Bergen County, N.J., proposes tax cut -- paper.</title>
<headline>Bergen County, N.J., proposes tax cut -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bergen County, N.J., officials proposed cutting property taxes for the fourth year in a row under a propsed budget for next year, the Bergen Record reported Thursday.</p>
<p>County Executive William Schuber unveiled a $446.7 million spending plan that is 0.8 percent higher than last year and calls for cutting 101 jobs from the 4,231-member work force, the paper said.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
